    "result_text": "Done. The full test suite is green.\n\n## What I implemented\n\nThe requirement: alongside the existing human-readable audit line, emit an **immutable structured event** via the `AUDIT` logger \u2014 `{seq, ownerId, customerCode, membershipLevel, event:'OWNER_CREATED'}` \u2014 carrying the owner's *current primary identifier*, designed so a later switch from `customerCode` to `memberId` flows through automatically.\n\nThree new files plus one pipeline edit:\n\n1. **`mapper/PrimaryIdentifier.java`** \u2014 single source of truth for \"the owner's current primary identifier.\" Returns `customerCode` today; when the code is unified into a `memberId`, only this one method changes and every consumer follows. Kept standalone (like `MembershipLevel`) so MapStruct doesn't treat it as an implicit mapping.\n\n2. **`rest/function/owner/OwnerCreatedEvent.java`** \u2014 an immutable `record` (deeply immutable, so the emitted event can't be altered) with a `toJson()` that renders the fields in the documented order, with proper JSON string escaping.\n\n3. **`rest/function/owner/LogOwnerCreatedEvent.java`** \u2014 the OfficeFloor step. A process-wide `AtomicInteger` gives the monotonically-increasing `seq` across creates; the identifier is sourced through `PrimaryIdentifier.of(owner)` and `membershipLevel` through `MembershipLevel.of(owner)` (same source of truth as the response DTO). Emits `AUDIT.info(event.toJson())`.\n\n4. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted an `auditEvent` step between the existing `audit` (line) step and `respond`, under the same `transaction` governance, so it runs after save (id available) and before the response.\n\nObserved output confirms both lines are emitted:\n```\nAUDIT - Owner created: id=11 customerCode=NSW-16E6609E ...\nAUDIT - {\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"customerCode\":\"NSW-16E6609E\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}\n```\n\nThe design keeps the JSON field/value routed through `PrimaryIdentifier`, so the \"so when the customerCode is unified into the memberId, the event carries the memberId instead\" future step is a one-line change with no consumer touching `getCustomerCode()` directly.\n\n`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS** (the repo contains a single test class, `AcceptanceTest`).",
